=== layout: one-panel

@body

![Inversion synapsis overview](repo:prototype/chromosome_assets/assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/inversion-synapsis.drawn.svg)

Gene-for-gene attraction in chromosome pairing (synapsis)

@citation

*C55 | Inversion synapsis: overview* - LECT13B, source slide 8 | Inversions

=== layout: one-panel

@body

![Inversion synapsis loop](repo:prototype/chromosome_assets/assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/inversion-synapsis-loop.drawn.svg)

The gene-for-gene pairing causes either the inversion chromosome or the wildtype chromosome to form a loop in the region in which the inversion chromosome has the inversion.

@citation

*C55 | Inversion synapsis: loop* - LECT13B, source slide 8 | Inversions

=== layout: one-panel

@body

![Paracentric anaphase](repo:prototype/chromosome_assets/assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/paracentric-anaphase.drawn.svg)

When the centromere is not included in the inverted region, one of the crossover products is a dicentric chromosome, and the reciprocal product is an acentric chromosome. Among the two chromatids not involved in the crossover, one carries the inversion and the other the normal gene sequence.

@citation

*C56 | Paracentric anaphase* - LECT13B, source slide 14 | Inversions

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Pericentric pairing](repo:prototype/chromosome_assets/assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/pericentric-pairing.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C57 | Pericentric pairing*

LECT13B, source slide 16 | Inversions

=== layout: one-panel

@body

![Pericentric anaphase](repo:prototype/chromosome_assets/assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/pericentric-anaphase.drawn.svg)

When the centromere is included in the inversion loop, one of the crossover products is duplicated for a and deficient for d; the other is duplicated for d and deficient for a. Among the two chromatids not involved in the crossover, one carries the inversion and the other is normal.

*C58 | Pericentric anaphase* - LECT13B, source slide 18 | Inversions

=== layout: one-panel

@body

![Inversion double-crossover problem](repo:prototype/chromosome_assets/assets/lect13b-chromo_alter_3-inversion/inversion-double-crossover-problem.drawn.svg)

First crossover: between B/b and C/c. Only the inverted region is shown paired; ends are unpaired.

@citation

*C59 | Inversion double-crossover problem* - LECT13B, source slide 22 | Inversions

